--- prepare nxcommand --slug nxb --role review
qargi: note: codex has only a partial read-only barrier on local: the Codex sandbox holds the shell commands of a member (read-only: no writes, workspace-write: the clone, its .git, OUT and TMPDIR only), not its reads: a member, read-only or not, can read whatever the account of the lead can read outside /dev, among it the real ~/.codex (its sessions and history and its configuration; the members' sign-in is the linked one, but the real auth.json is still a readable file), other repositories and keys; and not a hosted tool or an MCP server, which run outside the sandbox; no qargi guard hook runs: the publish and skill verbs are held only by the sandbox's write and network denial; the checks of the source showed shell writes refused and nothing more, so the claim stays partial
RUN=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX
ROLE=review
CLASS=read-only
PROFILE=review
MEMBER=reviewer
MODEL=gpt-6.1-sol
EFFORT=high
CLONE=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX/clone
OUT=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX/out
TMP=T/qargi-run.XXXXXX
GIT=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX/git
BASE_SHA=SHA
CONTRACT=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX/contract

TASK-BLOCK PATHS
RUN_DIR=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX
CLONE=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX/clone
OUT=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX/out
TMP=T/qargi-run.XXXXXX
GIT=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX/git
BASE_SHA=SHA
CONTRACT=T/scr/qargi.XXXXXX/contract
exit 0
